readme.fair:
Ticks are a pure function of the program, so they have to match exactly. Scores pass through each machine's BLAS, so they can differ in the last digits. Same seeds of `{fair_entry}`, each machine against {fair_reference}:

{fair_table}

The largest difference is {fair_max} bits per byte, about {fair_ratio} times below the record margin of 0.002, and a paired equivalence test against a tolerance of {tolerance} passes on every machine. Rerun the comparison with `python tools/fairness.py study/fairness/logs/*.json`, or run the matrix yourself with [the fairness workflow](.github/workflows/fairness.yml). In a browser the demo reads the same tick as native code.
